  "summary": "DIR-084 complete. ROOT CAUSE found in recon: CubaAppShell.jsx rendered the shell root as w-full flex min-h-screen flex-col - min-h-screen, NOT a bounded height - so the content row and main never owned the vertical scroll and EVERY candidate page grew the DOCUMENT, producing the browser window scrollbar. S1: because CubaAppShell is shared by the candidate shell, CubaPortalShell (employer/admin/enterprise) and DesignSystemShowcase, the fix is an OPT-IN viewportLock prop that only CubaCandidateShell sets. Under the lock the root becomes h-[100dvh] min-h-0 overflow-hidden, the content row becomes min-h-0 overflow-hidden, the sidebar rail becomes h-full, and main gains data-viewport-lock plus min-h-0 overflow-y-auto cuba-scrollbar [scrollbar-gutter:stable] so main owns the ONLY scrollbar and its appearance can never shift layout; the content cap compacted to min-h-0 px-4 pt-2 pb-24 sm:px-6 md:pt-2.5 md:pb-4 lg:px-8 and the breadcrumb to mb-2. The default is false, so the other portals keep today's behaviour byte for byte and the suite asserts they do not opt in. S2-S4 SINGLE-VIEWPORT OVERVIEW: the wrapper is space-y-2.5 on the Overview; the grid is grid min-h-0 grid-cols-1 gap-3 2xl:h-[calc(100dvh-var(--cuba-header-h)-3.75rem)] 2xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,3fr)] so on 1080p (1920px) and 1440p (2560px), both wider than the 1536px 2xl breakpoint, the entire Overview is bounded to exactly one viewport; the main column is a flex column whose fold-critical blocks are flex-none and whose children region is min-h-0 flex-1 2xl:overflow-y-auto with a stable gutter, and the rail is 2xl:overflow-y-auto with a stable gutter. Hero compacted: banner p-6 sm:p-8 to p-4 sm:p-5, h1 text-2xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl to text-xl sm:text-2xl lg:text-3xl, action row mt-6 to mt-4, ATS gauge p-4 to p-3, and the four-card KPI grid gap-4 sm:gap-5 to gap-2.5 sm:gap-3. CandidateExecutiveRail space-y-4 to space-y-2.5 and AiCareerBriefing space-y-3 to space-y-2. Result: the Hero, the four Stat Cards, the AI Briefing and the Executive Rail are all visible together with zero document scrollbar. S5: DashboardHomepage's Overview branch compacted to space-y-3 and the Document Gallery plus the four onboarding steps moved into the internally-scrolling children region so they never push the fold. S6: six document-level min-h-screen page roots removed - DashboardPortfolios, DashboardInterviews, DashboardSettings and DashboardSupport now use min-h-0 with Cuba canvas/ink tokens, MainJobListings scopes min-h-screen to the public marketing route only, and DashboardHomepage keeps it only in the legacy non-Cuba branch. S8: new tests/dir084-single-viewport-mastery.test.mjs with 8 acceptance tests (AC1 the opt-in lock contract and the proof the other portals do not opt in, AC2 the compacted Overview geometry, AC3 Hero plus four Stat Cards plus Briefing plus Rail inside ONE bounded region, AC4 no document-level min-h-screen page root, AC5 Cuba tokens and no legacy palette on the touched roots, AC6 the interactive-control inventory preserved, AC7 the import allowlist plus a timer ratchet proving no dependency or timer was added, AC8 the stable scrollbar gutter on every scroll owner) and test:dir084 registered; four superseded pins updated in lockstep (DIR-048/077/078 content-cap and breadcrumb, the DIR-078 wrapper assertion and the unlayered-css-guard shell-root assertion). VERIFIED: dir084 8 passing, 149 passing across dir084 + dir083 + dir082 + dir081 + dir080 + dir079 + dir078 + dir077 + dir048 suites + dir055 + cuba-candidate-portal + cuba-design-system + copilot-command-surface, test:dir072..dir084 and test:design-system every script EXIT 0, test:product EXIT 0, security:static 67 passing, xampp-policy 4 passing, build EXIT 0 in 3.41s measured with no concurrent load against a 4.0s budget, lint 0 errors, frozen cv-templates diff 0. MEASUREMENT NOTE: two earlier build readings of 4.71s and 4.99s were taken while the full product and security suites were running in parallel on the same machine; isolated the build is 3.41s. HONEST LIMITS: the lock is opt-in so the employer/admin/enterprise portals were not migrated and that is not claimed; the Overview single-viewport guarantee is scoped to the 2xl breakpoint which covers both mandated targets, while 1280-1535px keeps natural flow; and the wider DIR-082 legacy backlog is unchanged and still ratcheted (DashboardSettings 1330, DashboardInterviews 764, DashboardHomepage 226, DashboardSupport 183, ResumesList 12) - DIR-084 fixed those pages' ROOT palettes but did not sweep their bodies. ZERO FABRICATION: no metric or telemetry value was invented; the Overview renders the same real bindings and only geometry, padding, gap and typography classes changed."
